  "text_sample": "Your Page Title Copenhagen Gl\u00f8d Index Close No. Section 01 Home 02 Menus 03 Events 04 Private dining 05 Story No. Section 06 Journal 07 Gift cards 08 Visit 09 Book a table 10 All pages Find us J\u00e6gersborggade 41, 2200 K\u00f8benhavn N Open Wednesday to Saturday, 17:30 to 23:00 Talk to us [email protected] +00 00 00 00 00 Our story One fire since 2019 A wood-fire kitchen and natural wine bar on J\u00e6gersborggade, with one hearth and no gas in the kitchen. How it started How it started Meet the team Meet the team Opened 2019 Seats Twenty-eight Gas None in the kitchen Street J\u00e6gersborggade How it started A fire, a borrowed room and a menu on the back of a receipt Freja came home from Lofoten in 2018 with a notebook of recipes and no restaurant. She cooked pop-up dinners in a friend's bakery on J\u00e6gersborggade, on a grill she built from an old oil drum, and sold out every Sunday for a year. When the bakery moved, she took the lease, knocked out the ovens and built the hearth where they used to be. Gl\u00f8d means embers. The fire has not gone out on a service day since. Chef and owner Freja Lindqvist Grew up on Fan\u00f8, salting fish with her grandmother. She still does the Tuesday market run herself. Pr",
